# nr-office-ooxml-docx-parts: integration fragment

Two modules of the crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml): docx_parts (the Word package parts: pictures,
section properties, notes, comments and their sidecars, headers and footers, settings, tracked-change attributes, numbering)
and docx_runs (run normalisation and the settling of one story's tracked changes). No protocol method, service, Cargo
dependency or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to this task: every crate they use (mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js with its time::Tz,
mixdog-ooxml's own modules; dev: base64, tempfile) is already a dependency of mixdog-ooxml.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After the line `pub mod docx_revisions;` add:

    pub mod docx_parts;
    pub mod docx_runs;

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-docx-revisions (keep the list sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-parts.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-docx-parts/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "84d747f10a94a9e0f54aa48b106a8e4b3b1b568f15c02539fb2a639f130e594b",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-parts.mjs",
      "set": "office-docx-parts",
      "totalBytes": 542189
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-docx-parts/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool that
keeps this file reorders or reformats them.)

## Not compiled

The two modules, their unit tests and tests/twin_docx_parts.rs were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead):
the first build, cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml, is the check. The twin test replays native/core/fixtures/office-docx-parts and
needs no Node; twin_live_docx_parts (ignored) re-records through Node.
